%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
title: a2.1 Residents, family and staff
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Seven stakeholders. A resident (ST-01), often new to the home, meets, invites and walks with a fellow resident (ST-02). Three help them meet: the relative, who arranges the move and gives the life story (ST-03); the care worker, who receives newcomers and introduces residents (ST-04); the activity coordinator, who seats, introduces and pairs (ST-05). Medical and therapy staff assess and encourage walking (ST-06), and management runs admissions and staffing (ST-07). All share a concern for the resident's well-being and trust, and see the walk as an easy way to meet and stay active. They are divided on freedom against safety, and on what may be shared about a resident.

= Stakeholder - Resident with dementia [ST-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-01
|Name|Resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01 to SA-03.
|Type|Direct - moves in, meets others, invites, walks
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - company, friends
* HV-02 Dignity (high) - slips not exposed, not patronised
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - the truth from someone trusted, such as why they are here or who has died
* HV-01 Autonomy (high) - own choice of whom to meet and when to go out
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - own secrets, and a say in what others are told
* HV-07 Identity (high) - own past, own words
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - movement, fresh air, calm and a clear head
* HV-04 Safety (high) - no falls, no getting lost
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Arrives knowing nobody. Meets and invites ST-02. Family (ST-03) give the life story. Received and introduced by ST-04, ST-05. Walking assessed by ST-06.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-01 to SA-03; holds → HV-01 to HV-08; appears-in → PS-01 to PS-06; elaborated-as → HP-01, HP-02 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Fellow resident [ST-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-02
|Name|Fellow resident
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01 to SA-03.
|Type|Direct - meets ST-01, accepts or declines, walks. Often has dementia too.
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - a friend to talk to
* HV-01 Autonomy (high) - free to decline, or to end a walk
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - own secrets
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - movement, fresh air, calm
* HV-02 Dignity (medium) - not patronised
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Meets ST-01 by chance, or introduced by ST-04, ST-05. Own relatives, own care plan.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-02, SA-03; supports → SA-01; holds → HV-01 to HV-03, HV-05, HV-06; appears-in → PS-01, PS-03 to PS-05; elaborated-as → HP-01, HP-02 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Relative [ST-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-03
|Name|Relative
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01 to SA-03.
|Type|Indirect - arranges the move, gives the life story, agrees what may be shared, may consent for ST-01
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - their relative has company
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - no lies told to their relative
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - their relative settles and stays active
* HV-07 Identity (high) - their relative's life story known and respected
* HV-03 Privacy (low) - secrets shared with staff only
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Relative of ST-01. Gives the life story to ST-05. Agrees with ST-04 who answers painful questions.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01 to SA-03; holds → HV-03, HV-05 to HV-08; appears-in → PS-02, PS-05.

= Stakeholder - Care worker [ST-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-04
|Name|Care worker
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01 to SA-03.
|Type|Direct - receives newcomers, introduces residents, opens the garden door, answers painful questions
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - every resident back, unharmed
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - truthful answers, secrets kept
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - residents calm and active
* HV-06 Social connectedness (medium) - residents know each other
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - privacy in care
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Answers painful questions as agreed with ST-03. Tells ST-05 who gets along with whom. Follows ST-06 on walking and medical news.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01 to SA-03; holds → HV-03 to HV-06, HV-08; appears-in → PS-01 to PS-06; elaborated-as → HP-03 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Activity coordinator [ST-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-05
|Name|Activity coordinator
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01 to SA-03.
|Type|Direct - takes life stories, and seats, introduces and pairs residents
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-06 Social connectedness (high) - residents have company, and a walk eases first contact
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - residents active and calm
* HV-07 Identity (high) - life stories known and respected
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - life stories in their care
* HV-01 Autonomy (medium) - activities chosen by the resident
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Takes life stories with ST-01 and ST-03. Introduces and pairs ST-01 and ST-02. Learns from ST-04 who gets along with whom. Employed by ST-07.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01 to SA-03; holds → HV-01, HV-03, HV-05 to HV-07; appears-in → PS-03, PS-06.

= Stakeholder - Medical and therapy staff [ST-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-06
|Name|Medical and therapy staff (physician, nurse, physiotherapist, psychologist)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-03.
|Type|Indirect - assess walking, set walk length, encourage regular walks, tell medical news
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - fall risk
* HV-05 Well-being (high) - regular walking for fitness, mood and thinking
* HV-08 Truthfulness (high) - a diagnosis is told by them
* HV-03 Privacy (medium) - medical confidentiality
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Assess ST-01 and ST-02. Advise ST-04 and ST-05. Trusted person for medical topics.

== Graph edges ==

supports → SA-01, SA-03; holds → HV-03 to HV-05, HV-08; appears-in → PS-04.

= Stakeholder - Care home management [ST-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-07
|Name|Care home management
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Derived from SA-01, SA-03.
|Type|Indirect - runs admissions and staffing, controls exits and data, decides on adopting the System
|Values and motivations|(((
* HV-04 Safety (high) - liable for falls and exits
* HV-03 Privacy (high) - GDPR, health data
* HV-05 Well-being (medium) - quality of care
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Employs ST-04 and ST-05. Admits ST-01. Responsible for the garden and the exits.

== Graph edges ==

governs → SA-01 (admission, exits), SA-03 (staffing), System data; holds → HV-03 to HV-05.
